  "id": "DrugBank_DB00413 - MONDO_10482",
  "verbalization": "Pramipexole is implicated in the pathogenesis of X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome through a multi-step mechanism involving the treatment of Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease (HLOPD), a condition that is linked to the syndrome. The evidence suggests that Pramipexole, through its indication for HLOPD, may exert a therapeutic effect on the underlying pathology of X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome. This is supported by the presence of intermediate entities—Pimavanserin, Istradefylline, and Tolcapone—that are also indicated for HLOPD and are connected to the target syndrome. These drugs are known to modulate dopamine signaling, which is a key pathway in Parkinson’s disease, and their involvement in the pathway implies a potential mechanism of action that could be relevant to X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of dopamine modulation in the pathophysiology of the syndrome, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, but further research is needed to confirm the direct relationship between Pramipexole and the syndrome.",
